; freq-check-model.form — research direction for response attunement.
; A predicate result, a trained-model evaluation and a person's experience are
; distinct evidence. Read current source and receipts before claiming a lane.

(freq-check-model
  (what
    "Explore a native model that reads a candidate response in the context of"
    "the offered request and helps revise it toward trust, sovereignty and vitality."
    "Architecture and size follow measured task performance; they do not establish"
    "semantic understanding or readiness by themselves.")

  (in-the-loop
    (voice "The dialogue covenant guides generation: attend to the request and keep meaning with the person.")
    (sense "Inspect what the implemented predicate or model actually evaluates.")
    (revise "Revise only what serves the request; preserve facts, uncertainty, boundaries and the person's words."))

  (implementation
    (head "form/form/form-stdlib/form-freq-check.fk is a bounded predicate; inspect its current inputs.")
    (candidates embedding-as-recipe.fk attention.fk transformer-block.fk
                transformer-numerics.fk tensor-quant.fk jit-tensor-emit.fk language-model.fk)
    (evidence "Native primitives establish their checked operations. A trained response-quality model needs"
              "its own weights, held-out evaluation and serving receipt."))

  (training
    "Use selected request/response/revision excerpts with separately established"
    "capture, destination, retention and training scope. Ordinary feedback can simply"
    "change the current encounter. A person may offer an explanation, a preferred reply"
    "or a brief verdict; naming a difficulty is optional."
    "Legacy clear/fear labels and tc-gold-named are compatibility interfaces, not a"
    "required vocabulary for people. Inspect the actual recording door before using it."
    "Automatic labels are hypotheses. Preserve concrete consequential information in"
    "revisions and evaluate on new examples outside the training selection.")

  (learning
    "Routing and capture alone do not demonstrate improvement. Record selected data,"
    "training effects and independent evaluation separately. Keep personal material"
    "outside public artifacts. Existing capture and withdrawal controls need their own"
    "implementation proof; this teaching does not change them.")

  (discipline
    "Attention is a response practice. Measurements state method, source and scope."
    "Keep room for play, acknowledgment, practical help and a complete pause."))
